<p>Use this dialog box to configure the settings for paper loaded in the 
 paper trays.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="inputtray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select an input tray. If you select an optionally installed tray, be 
 sure to specify the tray in the <span class="Term-Soft">Options</span> group.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="size" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Size:</span></p>
<p>Select a paper size for the tray you have selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Input 
 Tray:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="type" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type:</span></p>
<p>Select a type of paper loaded in the tray.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Plain &amp; Recycled (Auto. for Postcard)</span>, it is normally printed as plain paper/recycled paper. If the print paper size is postcard, print with a paper type suitable for postcards.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="autotray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not Use Auto Tray Select</span></p>
<p>Select the check box if the selected paper tray is set as unavailable 
 for the Auto Tray Select function at the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="position" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Paper Position</span></p>
<p>Select the direction of paper loaded.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="update" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Modify Input Tray/Paper Size</span></p>
<p>Click to update <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray Settings List:</span> 
 with the information in <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Size:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Paper Type:</span> 
 and<span class="Term-Soft"> Paper Position</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="list" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray Settings List:</span></p>
<p>Lists input trays and the size of paper loaded.</p>
<p>To add a new entry, select an input tray, paper size, paper type and 
 paper position, and then click <span class="Term-Soft">Modify Input Tray/Paper 
 Size</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the entries and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
